==Strategy==
Prepare for an intense battle! Unlike its [[Crazed Titan Cat (Enemy)|Crazed]] and [[Manic Jamiera Cat (Enemy)|Manic]] counterparts, Li'l Jamiera Cat has a 90% chance of doing a [[Wave Attack]], and on top of the much higher Wave Attack chance, the {{4c}} restrictions remove most Wave Blockers and Wave Immune units. Li'l Jamiera Cat's long Wave Attack is especially deadly when considering that most Special and Rare units have slow speed, such as [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]].

There is one way to mitigate the Wave damage though, it is to '''lure Li'l Jamiera near the [[Cat Base]]'''. Because the Cats won't be active for as long before reaching Jamiera, they won't take as much chip damage from his Waves.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Ancient Egg: N001 (Special Cat)|Haniwa Cat]]: Haniwa Cat is even more effective than Ramen Cat on this stage because it consists solely of Traitless enemies. Haniwa Cat has higher health, lower cost and lower recharge, but is also harder to obtain and is slower. They can survive 2 hits from Li'l Jamiera at Lv.34, but getting them to Lv.40 is recommended so that they can tank some hits from the Gories as well.
*[[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]]: Although this stage contains no Angels, Ramen Cat is still effective because of his spammability and high health. He can survive 2 hits from Li'l Jamiera at Lv.40+2, so leveling him up to that point is strongly advised.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Kung Fu Cat (Special Cat)|Dancer Cat]]: Dancer Cat with the [[Immune to Waves]] Talent does extremely well on this stage. He does only barely outrange Li'l Jamiera, but he makes up for that with a faster attack rate than Musashi, and a much shorter recharge, which allows him to be stacked en masse. His Talent does cost a bit of NP though, costing 125 for Attack Buff and 75 for Wave Immunity.
*[[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Supercat]]: Supercat's [[Wave Shield]] isn't actually his selling point here. He can [[weaken]] Traitless enemies, and since he has a lot of knockbacks, he can hit Li'l Jamiera with the weaken repeatedly, allowing you to complete the stage much easier. If one is able to time him to hit a peon in order to stay out of Li'l Jamiera's range, his Wave Shield is usable due to not being knocked back by Li'l Jamiera's attack. His true form, Ironcat is recommended to further increase his survivability thanks to the addition of the Resist ability.
*[[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Green Shell Cat]]: This Cat at first seems like it would be harmful to bring, repeatedly triggering Li'l Jamiera's wave attacks, but it's surprisingly tanky. If you bring Wave Immune attackers, you can use Green Shell Cat to pin Li'l Jamiera back. It is not recommended to use this unit if you don't have Wave Immune attackers.
*[[Miyamoku Musashi (Special Cat)|Miyamoku Musashi]]: Musashi is a backliner with Wave Immunity, making him a great pick for this stage since he outranges Li'l Jamiera by a wide margin. Beware his 9-second attack rate, which gives plenty of time for Gories to rush in between his attacks.
*[[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: With Supercat's weaken, he can get quite a few hits off and contribute a lot of damage before dying.
*Talented [[Li'l Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Mohawk Cat]]: When given the Wave Immunity Talent, Li'l Mohawk becomes a great meatshield for this stage since they're completely unharmed by Li'l Jamiera's Waves. Bringing [[Mini-Saurus (Combo)|Mini-Saurus]] also decreases their own recharge to 2 seconds, on top of affecting other spammable units like Ramen Cat, so it is strongly recommended.
*[[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Glass Cat]]/[[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Vendor Cat and Kitten]]: Both are crowd-controllers that can knockback Li'l Jamiera if he starts attacking the Cat Base. Note that they're both Single Attack, meaning that they will waste attacks on peons if not used carefully. Vendor Cat will also stick around, unlike Glass Cat, which means that they'll push Li'l Jamiera back further. This can be useful if timed properly with Awakened Bahamut to prolong Bahamut's lifespan by delaying Li'l Jamiera's attack.
*[[Jagando Jr. (Special Cat)|Lord of Ruin Jagando Jr.]]: He may not be Immune to Waves, however, his Strong Against allows him to survive many Wave Attacks sent out by Jamiera, and doubled if weakened by Mightycat. His Knockback can also regain ground if you desperately need it.
*[[Yellow Nyanko Ranger]]: Its utility comes from [[Yellow Strike (Combo)|its combo]], which grants all [[:Category:Nyanko Rangers|Nyanko Rangers]] Immunity to Waves. He is best paired with other Nyanko Rangers, as this will net you the most value from his combo. However, note that the only Rangers who outrange Li'l Jamiera Cat are [[Fedora Cat (Special Cat)|Blue Nyanko Ranger]] and [[Goggles Cat (Special Cat)|Green Nyanko Ranger]], the latter being a crowd-controller with pitifully low DPS.

